| A module written in `code` keeps the class of a particle it was sent, and
| reads it back on the next call.
|
| `kept = particle._class` is the natural line for a program that remembers
| what it was last asked. As a program of its own it is fine — the value is
| the program's. Linked as a module, the particle came from the linking
| program's dispatch, and once the call returns that program is done with
| it; what the module kept points into memory that was somebody else's.
|
| Found 2026-09-18 in a program that links other programs at runtime: a
| class name kept this way read back as noise on the next call, and a whole
| particle kept the same way ended the process. The module is
| `native_modules/test_keeper.code`, built to a `.so` by the fixture runner
| with `--target shared`, the same build any linked program gets.

link "native_modules/test_keeper.so" as m

emit NoteClass { particle = TasksDelta { added = [] } } to m get noted
assert noted ∈ Noted

emit RecallClass to m get back
assert back ∈ Recalled
assert back.class = "TasksDelta"
